<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galeazzo Maria Sforza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1444–1476</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galeazzo Maria Sforza was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from 1466 to 1476, eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-sforza">Francesco Sforza</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bianca-maria-visconti">Bianca Maria Visconti</a>. He kept a lavish court, patronised music and art, and married his illegitimate daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caterina-sforza">Caterina Sforza</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girolamo-riario">Girolamo Riario</a>. Hated for his cruelty and excesses, he was assassinated by three Milanese nobles in the church of Santo Stefano on 26 December 1476.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galeazzo-maria-sforza.jpg" alt="Galeazzo Maria Sforza" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Piero del Pollaiuolo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piero_Pollaiuolo_Portrait_of_Galeazzo_Maria_Sforza.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
